<section id="comments">
  <h2>Comments (5)</h2>

  
    <a id="comment-4985" class="header-offset"></a>
    <article>
      <header>
        <p><a href="/tag/0F0V#comment-4985">Comment #4985</a>
        by
        <cite>Noah Olander</cite>
        on <time datetime="2020-03-16 16:15:38.834442">March 16, 2020 at 16:15 </time>
      </header>

      <blockquote><p>There's a typo right before you write down the E2 page of the spectral sequence: You should write <script type="math/tex">R^p g_*R^q j_*\mathcal{F}=0</script> for <script type="math/tex">p&gt;2</script> instead of <script type="math/tex">R^pj_* \mathcal{F}</script>. </p></blockquote>
    </article>
  
    <a id="comment-4995" class="header-offset"></a>
    <article>
      <header>
        <p><a href="/tag/0F0V#comment-4995">Comment #4995</a>
        by
        <cite>Noah Olander</cite>
        on <time datetime="2020-03-18 11:52:32.796324">March 18, 2020 at 11:52 </time>
      </header>

      <blockquote><p>I think when you write "On the other hand, by Theorem 03Q9 we have <script type="math/tex">R^2f_*\mathcal{F}_{\overline{\eta}} = H^2 ( \mathbf{A}^1_{\overline{\eta}} , \mathcal{F})</script>, you mean <script type="math/tex">\eta</script> is the generic point of <script type="math/tex">\mathbf{A}^{d-1}</script> but you don't say what <script type="math/tex">\eta</script> is. </p></blockquote>
    </article>
  
    <a id="comment-5230" class="header-offset"></a>
    <article>
      <header>
        <p><a href="/tag/0F0V#comment-5230">Comment #5230</a>
        by
        <cite><a href="https://math.columbia.edu/~dejong" rel="author">Johan</a></cite>
        
        on <time datetime="2020-06-11 11:03:48.184550">June 11, 2020 at 11:03 </time>
      </header>

      <blockquote><p>Thanks and both are fixed <a href="https://github.com/stacks/stacks-project/commit/cbfcabf1e5629c6650e513b63c0d2939ae8e6cd1">here</a>.</p></blockquote>
    </article>
  
    <a id="comment-8286" class="header-offset"></a>
    <article>
      <header>
        <p><a href="/tag/0F0V#comment-8286">Comment #8286</a>
        by
        <cite>Xiaolong Liu</cite>
        on <time datetime="2023-03-30 21:13:22.283503">March 30, 2023 at 21:13 </time>
      </header>

      <blockquote><p>In "Interlude I", we should write "Choose a local equation <script type="math/tex">f\in\mathfrak{m}_y\subset \mathscr{O}_{Y,y}</script>" instead of "Choose a local equation <script type="math/tex">f\in\mathfrak{m}_y=\mathscr{O}_{Y,y}</script>". (Please delete the comment above)</p></blockquote>
    </article>
  
    <a id="comment-8917" class="header-offset"></a>
    <article>
      <header>
        <p><a href="/tag/0F0V#comment-8917">Comment #8917</a>
        by
        <cite><a href="https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/" rel="author">Stacks project</a></cite>
        
        on <time datetime="2024-04-10 12:53:01.422262">April 10, 2024 at 12:53 </time>
      </header>

      <blockquote><p>Thanks and fixed <a href="https://github.com/stacks/stacks-project/commit/3edffc06ca87b94d36ebda5d600aa8daf02a7719">here</a>.</p></blockquote>
    </article>
  

  
